 "name": "Core Reversal",
 "type": "feat",
 "img": "modules/jjk5e/icons/techniques/triple-core.svg",
 "system": {
  "description": {
   "value": "<p><em>Triple Core — Cursed Technique Reversal</em></p><p>With great mastery over Reversed Cursed Technique, you have found the reversal of your technique, allowing you to reverse the functions of your cores, allowing you to enter one of the following forms as a bonus action. You cannot use a Core form with Core Reversal.</p>\n<p><strong>Blocking Blows.</strong> : When you are hit with a melee attack, you can spend 2 CE to gain resistance to that damage.</p>\n<p><strong>Reverse Energy Blast.</strong> : As an action you spend CE to launch a blast of reverse cursed energy. You make a ranged cursed energy attack against a target within 160 feet dealing 4d6 radiant damage for every 2 CE.</p>\n<p><strong>Offensive Form.</strong> : As a bonus action, you assume this form for 1 minute, buffing your offense. You deal additional damage equal to 2 times your current cursed energy and costing 2 CE at the beginning of your turn to maintain.</p>\n<p><strong>Crash.</strong> : When you hit a creature with a melee attack, they are affected by your technique and cannot control their speed. If a creature moves more than 20 feet on their turn, they must make a Dexterity saving throw or fall prone.</p>",
   "chat": ""
  },
